In strange-mark.polite, line 1:

    please show 1 @ 2
                  ^

I do not know what to do with `@` here.

PoliteLang is written in words. The only marks it uses are quotes
for text, a colon to open a block, brackets for grouping, a comma,
and the arithmetic signs + - * / > < >= <=.

If you meant it as part of some text, put it in quotes:

    please show "@"

In strange-mark.polite, line 1:

    please show 1 @ 2
                    ^

This is missing a `please`.

Out here at the top of the file, every request asks for itself.
Inside a block you only have to ask once, when you open it.

Ask, and I will happily do it:

    please ...

In strange-mark.polite, line 1:

    please show 1 @ 2
                    ^

I do not know what is being asked for here.

Every request starts with a word I know. `polite words` lists them
all, and `polite explain "..."` says what one means.

The everyday words are a good place to start:

    please show "hello"
